**Directory creation legend:**

- `[bootstrap]` — eagerly created (empty) by `omr-bootstrap` at workspace init.
  The directory shell exists immediately; *contents* are populated on-demand by
  the skill noted in the comment (e.g. `docs/survey/` is filled when
  `omr-synthesis` runs in survey mode).
- `[on-demand]` — created lazily by a specific skill when first needed. No
  workspace directories currently use this strategy; all dirs above are
  pre-created by bootstrap.

**Note on `skills/`:** Skill contracts (8 JSON files) and built-in pattern
definitions are **not** copied into the workspace. They remain in the installed
`omr-core` skill package and are read at runtime. Only mutable workspace state
(`tree-state.json`) lives under `.omr/`.

